**The cutting plane.** It passes through $O$, is parallel to $AD$ (the $x$-axis), and makes $60^\circ$ with the base. A plane parallel to the $x$-axis has normal $\mathbf n=(0,a,b)$. The angle with the base (normal $\mathbf k$) satisfies
$$\frac{|b|}{\sqrt{a^2+b^2}}=\cos 60^\circ=\tfrac12 \;\Longrightarrow\; a^2=3b^2.$$
Taking $\mathbf n=(0,\sqrt3,1)$, the plane through $O$ is
